---
---A session's full transcript, merged across all of its checkpoints. When the session has been shared, it is served from that public snapshot, so it stays readable after sharing.
---
---Use an own-account bearer token (including supported service accounts) or a Core-issued plugin installation bearer token, subject to the permissions and restrictions below. Plugin assertion JWTs and plugin OAuth user-delegation tokens are not accepted here.
---
---Live reads require pull on the repository storing the checkpoint payload (contents:read for plugin installations). Other authorized automation principals are accepted. Separate public/share exceptions: with no bearer, X-Anon-Repo supports public-repository reads when anonymous signing is configured; the storage repository must be readable for live content. A caller without storage-repository access, including a tokenless caller without X-Anon-Repo, may instead read an existing visible share snapshot, even for a private repository. Missing or disabled shares return 404; access-check failures do not fall back to snapshots. These exceptions are outside the user/plugin credential labels.
---
