---Resolve sessions' effective display names and list rows
---
---Resolves a batch of session ids to their effective display names and full list rows, read live from the sessions table. `names` maps each known id to its resolved name (custom override, then AI-generated, then the heuristic); `sessions` maps it to the same item shape the sessions list returns. Unknown ids are absent from both maps, so callers keep whatever fallback they already hold. Built for search-result hydration: the search index stores only index-time heuristics, and this read overlays the current names and row data at query time. Row items carry the stored ingest-time author login; this read performs no live identity resolve (the search caller renders authors from its own index), so it stays cell-local.
---
---`POST /api/v1/repos/{repo_id}/sessions:resolve-names`
---@param input entire.sessions.ResolveSessionNamesRequest
---@return entire.sessions.SessionNamesResolveResult? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:resolve_session_names(input) end

---Resolve sessions' display names and list rows across repos
---
---The cross-repo batch form of the per-repo sessions:resolve-names: one call resolves session display names (and, with include:["rows"], full list rows) for every repo group on a search page, keyed by the requested repo id. Authorization is per repo — a repo the caller cannot read (including its checkpoint-storage repo when that is separate), that this region does not host, or whose read failed is silently absent from the response, and its ids must be treated as unanswered, not as authoritatively absent. Session ids unknown to a RESOLVED repo are absent from that repo's maps, which IS authoritative. The total session ids across all groups is capped at 500 (one search page). Row items carry the stored ingest-time author login; this read performs no live identity resolve (the search caller renders authors from its own index), so it stays cell-local.
---
---`POST /api/v1/sessions:resolve-names`
---@param input entire.sessions.ResolveSessionNamesBatchRequest
---@return entire.sessions.SessionNamesBatchResolveOutputBody? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:resolve_session_names_batch(input) end

